course: dictionary
lesson: 5512
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and leaf is a good example. When you meet it, look at the words around it. «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter» is about plant parts, because the hedgehog is lying in a heap on the ground.
explain: «She lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves» is also about plant parts. Other sentences use leaf differently. If someone says they leaf through a book, they are turning its pages, not picking anything off a tree. Always try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A leaf is one of the flat, usually green parts that grow on a plant or tree.
fact: A leaf is also one sheet of paper in a book, with a page on each side.
fact: To leaf through a book means to turn its pages quickly without reading closely.
fact: Leaves make food for a plant from sunlight, water and air. This is called photosynthesis.
fact: To turn over a new leaf means to start behaving better.
exercise: «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter.» What are the leaves here? | *Plant parts lying on the ground | Pages from a book | Sheets of paper in a notebook | Flat pieces that make a table bigger
exercise: Jess says, «She began to leaf through the book.» What does leaf through mean? | *To turn the pages quickly without reading closely | To tear out the pages | To read every word very slowly | To glue the pages together
exercise: Sam stopped being rude and started helping everyone, so his teacher says he has turned over a new leaf. What does this mean? | He started growing new leaves | He found a leaf on the path | *He started behaving better | He turned the pages of his book
test: «A leaf of the table was pulled out so that more people could sit down.» What is a leaf of a table? | A flat green part of a plant | *An extra flat piece that makes the table bigger | A branch that has fallen off | A page with words on both sides
test: In science, leaves make food for the plant from sunlight, water and air. What is this process called? | *Photosynthesis | Hibernation | Camouflage | Pollination
exam: «The satanic leaf-tailed gecko has a body and tail that look like a dry curled leaf.» What does the gecko's body look like? | A pile of sticks | A green snake | A bright red flower | *A dry curled leaf
